    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45 degrees incidence. Initialize from quarter-wave thicknesses at 675 nm center wavelength. Apply gradient thickness optimization with perturbation schedule: layers 0-3 receive ±25 nm initial step magnitude, layers 4-23 receive ±10 nm initial step magnitude. Target high reflectance in 450-650 nm band and high transmittance in 700-1000 nm band. Evaluate unpolarized light (average of s and p polarization). Maximum 24 layers fixed. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
